WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.724 --> 00:00:04.874
Welcome to Ear Biscuits,

00:00:04.874 --> 00:00:07.332
the podcast where two
lifelong friends talk

00:00:07.332 --> 00:00:09.267
about life for a long time.

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:10.100
I'm Rhett.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.396
And I'm Link.

00:00:11.396 --> 00:00:13.688
This week at the brown
table of dim lighting,

00:00:13.688 --> 00:00:16.646
We're taking you on a
journey that we've been

00:00:16.646 --> 00:00:18.104
on for many months,

00:00:18.104 --> 00:00:19.863
this culminated in this,

00:00:19.863 --> 00:00:22.735
I was going to say huge TikTok project,

00:00:22.735 --> 00:00:25.193
but basically it's... in our minds,

00:00:25.193 --> 00:00:27.278
We've put a lot of energy into this thing.

00:00:27.278 --> 00:00:28.822
That's just come out.

00:00:28.822 --> 00:00:29.655
Don't oversell it.

00:00:29.655 --> 00:00:30.488
We know how it went.

00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:31.821
This past Friday. But, yeah.

00:00:31.821 --> 00:00:33.377
As of the recording of this,

00:00:33.377 --> 00:00:37.272
we haven't experienced what
you have now experienced,

00:00:37.272 --> 00:00:42.092
which is watching our, we,
we've been calling it Hazel.

00:00:42.092 --> 00:00:43.500
That's what we call the project.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.333
Yeah.

00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:45.374
Our Hazel TikTok...

00:00:45.374 --> 00:00:47.159
Our multi project, multipart

00:00:47.159 --> 00:00:48.909
one night scripted...

00:00:51.598 --> 00:00:53.348
horror comedy series.

00:00:55.577 --> 00:00:56.410
Yeah.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.777
I know, when you're dealing
with these new mediums,

00:00:58.777 --> 00:01:01.377
you don't know exactly
how to, to describe it,

00:01:01.377 --> 00:01:02.950
but what we will say,

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:05.872
if you are listening right now,

00:01:05.872 --> 00:01:06.705
They are.

00:01:06.705 --> 00:01:10.164
And you did not already watch
what we're talking about,

00:01:10.164 --> 00:01:11.608
because you're like, you
didn't know about it,

00:01:11.608 --> 00:01:14.359
or you're like, I don't
do to TikTok thing.

00:01:14.359 --> 00:01:18.797
It will be more of an
enjoyable experience for you.

00:01:18.797 --> 00:01:22.750
If you drop what you're doing
and take the time to watch it.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.958
Even if you're not a TikTok person.

00:01:24.958 --> 00:01:28.021
Now, at some point, we
are going to post it on,

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.326
depending on when you're
listening to this,

00:01:29.326 --> 00:01:30.409
it will be on our,

00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:32.207
the Rhett and Link YouTube
channel at some point,

00:01:32.207 --> 00:01:34.040
just in its full form.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.290
Which will make it
easier if you don't want

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:38.938
to use, you know, the TikTok app.

00:01:38.938 --> 00:01:39.771
But anyway,

00:01:39.771 --> 00:01:42.079
we just suggest that you
go over and watch it.

00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:43.162
I dunno. It's a little...

00:01:43.162 --> 00:01:44.802
We're going to be talking about it so,

00:01:44.802 --> 00:01:45.635
you need to have a little...

00:01:45.635 --> 00:01:47.805
It's a little over like
20 minutes of your time

00:01:47.805 --> 00:01:51.050
that you would have to devote to the full,

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:53.646
the full experience and that
it would just be helpful

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.315
to then come back and be able to hear the,

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:56.647
the discussion about it.

00:01:56.647 --> 00:02:00.174
I use the term ambitious
in, in the creative realm.

00:02:00.174 --> 00:02:01.507
It's something that, like, we can get

00:02:01.507 --> 00:02:04.768
into all the reasons
why we decided to do it.

00:02:04.768 --> 00:02:07.449
There's a number of itches
that we wanted to scratch.

00:02:07.449 --> 00:02:09.865
And boy, I really want to
know what people think.

00:02:09.865 --> 00:02:11.448
We can talk about the anticipation.

00:02:11.448 --> 00:02:13.181
That's another part of
this that has been so fun.

00:02:13.181 --> 00:02:15.514
But another thing we want to talk about,

00:02:15.514 --> 00:02:19.968
kinda, a larger conversation
than just the Hazel project

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:22.705
is our relationship with TikTok.

00:02:22.705 --> 00:02:23.538
Mhm.

00:02:23.538 --> 00:02:26.880
And, you know, having come up on YouTube,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.455
having 15 years of
figuring out how to take

00:02:30.455 --> 00:02:32.394
what we want to do and translate it

00:02:32.394 --> 00:02:34.989
into the particular platforms where we

00:02:34.989 --> 00:02:38.035
can get traction and
where there's audience,

00:02:38.035 --> 00:02:40.418
and then the advent of
TikTok and figuring out

00:02:40.418 --> 00:02:44.136
well, what's, what does
mythical on TikTok mean?

00:02:44.136 --> 00:02:44.969
Yeah.

00:02:44.969 --> 00:02:46.196
What are the opportunities there?

00:02:46.196 --> 00:02:48.446
We've been through a lot of

00:02:49.563 --> 00:02:52.952
challenges as we tried to figure that out.

00:02:52.952 --> 00:02:54.996
So I think that, in and of itself,

00:02:54.996 --> 00:02:56.369
can, can be a fun conversation.

00:02:56.369 --> 00:03:01.210
So, if you're an avid
TikToker or watcher of TikTok,

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:02.673
or if you have nothing to do with it,

00:03:02.673 --> 00:03:05.756
I think there's going to be
touch points for all of us to,

00:03:05.756 --> 00:03:09.923
to figure out how we
interface with that platform.

00:03:11.258 --> 00:03:12.438
Because you may find yourself,

00:03:12.438 --> 00:03:14.580
you might be, I think
this is our tendency,

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:15.927
maybe just because of our age,

00:03:15.927 --> 00:03:18.507
it's just like when a new social
media platform comes along,

00:03:18.507 --> 00:03:19.408
you just are like,

00:03:19.408 --> 00:03:22.347
"Uh, really? Like, this is the thing now?

00:03:22.347 --> 00:03:23.723
Like, am I going to
have to get an account?"

00:03:23.723 --> 00:03:25.981
And then at some point,
based on your personality,

00:03:25.981 --> 00:03:28.813
your disposition, and the way
that you divide your time,

00:03:28.813 --> 00:03:30.261
there's a point, there's a threshold

00:03:30.261 --> 00:03:32.232
for most people in
which they either decide

00:03:32.232 --> 00:03:34.289
to swear it off and never join,

00:03:34.289 --> 00:03:36.281
or they finally give in and join.

00:03:36.281 --> 00:03:40.176
And I think that as middle aged creators,

00:03:40.176 --> 00:03:44.268
there's an interesting, with
kids who enjoy this medium,

00:03:44.268 --> 00:03:46.601
it's sort of an interesting
conversation around

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.810
how do you make a decision
to actually go for it?

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.384
Why do you do it? What's your approach?

00:03:50.384 --> 00:03:52.438
What are you learning? What
are you trying to accomplish?

00:03:52.438 --> 00:03:53.740
Right.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:58.145
But let's start with
this, the idea for Hazel,

00:03:58.145 --> 00:04:00.443
and kind of what was, what was behind it?

00:04:00.443 --> 00:04:04.178
What set the stage in your recollection?

00:04:04.178 --> 00:04:06.264
Because it was, it was many months ago.

00:04:06.264 --> 00:04:07.097
Yeah, well.

00:04:07.097 --> 00:04:08.888
It wasn't first, like
let's do something for,

00:04:08.888 --> 00:04:10.203
let's do something scary.
Do something for Halloween.

00:04:10.203 --> 00:04:11.036
There was something, there,

00:04:11.036 --> 00:04:15.139
there was conversation that
was going on in the background.

00:04:15.139 --> 00:04:18.488
Which is, as we've established,

00:04:18.488 --> 00:04:20.196
And we actually did a whole episode

00:04:20.196 --> 00:04:21.541
about it earlier this year,

00:04:21.541 --> 00:04:22.999
where we, we talked about
all the other things

00:04:22.999 --> 00:04:25.309
that we have worked on,

00:04:25.309 --> 00:04:28.267
that you've never seen because it's...

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:32.849
Their ideas that are developed
for television or movies.

00:04:32.849 --> 00:04:35.307
That is a whole different process outside

00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:39.724
of the digital media that
we kind of own and control,

00:04:40.725 --> 00:04:42.702
which is the thing that
you're watching right now.

00:04:42.702 --> 00:04:45.458
Which, we don't have to ask
permission to make this podcast.

00:04:45.458 --> 00:04:46.291
No one has to approve it.

00:04:46.291 --> 00:04:48.168
So, those things where
you're writing scripts

00:04:48.168 --> 00:04:49.911
and trying to get traditional
stuff out the ground,

00:04:49.911 --> 00:04:52.800
it's there, it's a long time coming

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.140
and then it may never show up.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.473
No one may ever see it.

00:04:55.473 --> 00:04:57.181
And that's very frustrating for us.

00:04:57.181 --> 00:04:58.829
There's so much, even right now,

00:04:58.829 --> 00:05:02.048
like even, just so you know, right now,

00:05:02.048 --> 00:05:06.148
we're in the midst of working on a couple

00:05:06.148 --> 00:05:08.986
of very exciting projects.

00:05:08.986 --> 00:05:10.713
I'll just go ahead and
say, one's a, I mean,

00:05:10.713 --> 00:05:12.671
we've got multiple TV
shows that we've tried

00:05:12.671 --> 00:05:14.081
to get off the ground and continue to try

00:05:14.081 --> 00:05:15.628
to get off the ground, but there's a,

00:05:15.628 --> 00:05:18.599
another pilot that we have completed.

00:05:18.599 --> 00:05:20.708
And now there's a, a feature script,

00:05:20.708 --> 00:05:24.153
a whole movie that we are
beginning to, to write.

00:05:24.153 --> 00:05:27.414
And so, these are things
that we are passionate about

00:05:27.414 --> 00:05:29.488
and their, it's a fun process.

00:05:29.488 --> 00:05:33.494
And we throw ourselves creatively
at them and hopefully one,

00:05:33.494 --> 00:05:35.761
or multiple of them,
will be able to be made.

00:05:35.761 --> 00:05:37.248
And I think when you look at the,

00:05:37.248 --> 00:05:39.686
sort of the pie chart of our
time, when you wonder, like,

00:05:39.686 --> 00:05:41.421
what do Rhett and Link do?

00:05:41.421 --> 00:05:42.657
Like, well, what do they do besides

00:05:42.657 --> 00:05:44.435
the things that I see them do?

00:05:44.435 --> 00:05:45.268
Mhm.

00:05:45.268 --> 00:05:46.490
There's a big piece of the pie.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.963
That's like doesn't result
in things that you see.

00:05:48.963 --> 00:05:51.773
So, because that's,
it's frustrating, right?

00:05:51.773 --> 00:05:52.606
At least yet.

00:05:52.606 --> 00:05:56.297
It's frustrating to kind of
pour yourself into something.

00:05:56.297 --> 00:05:59.411
So then, the conversation
sort of shifted to a place

00:05:59.411 --> 00:06:00.861
where it's like, okay, yes.

00:06:00.861 --> 00:06:02.231
We've got all this
stuff we're trying to do

00:06:02.231 --> 00:06:03.736
that may never get seen.

00:06:03.736 --> 00:06:06.300
We've got all this
stuff that we already do

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.356
that does get seen on a regular basis,

00:06:09.356 --> 00:06:10.410
but is there an in-between?

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:12.162
Can we put one more thing on our plate,

00:06:12.162 --> 00:06:13.462
which is the in-between,

00:06:13.462 --> 00:06:15.170
which is stuff that has a high,

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:18.441
sort of creative, experimental quotient.

00:06:18.441 --> 00:06:23.091
Trying something new that
is more narrative maybe

00:06:23.091 --> 00:06:25.674
in, in, in, in its description.

00:06:26.717 --> 00:06:28.020
Is there another, is there
a place for us to do that?

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:31.538
Yeah, because we're developing
this narrative content.

00:06:31.538 --> 00:06:32.371
Yeah.

00:06:32.371 --> 00:06:34.346
How do we do some of that,
that people can actually see?

00:06:34.346 --> 00:06:36.652
And also do it in a very self-contained,

00:06:36.652 --> 00:06:39.183
frankly cheap way that doesn't take a lot

00:06:39.183 --> 00:06:42.396
of our time and doesn't
take a lot of money.

00:06:42.396 --> 00:06:43.229
So.

00:06:43.229 --> 00:06:47.937
And, also, then is structured
so that it makes us part

00:06:47.937 --> 00:06:50.296
of a different conversation.

00:06:50.296 --> 00:06:51.129
Yeah.

00:06:51.129 --> 00:06:51.962
You know, if you're,

00:06:51.962 --> 00:06:53.920
if you're an avid
listener of Ear Biscuits,

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:57.573
if you're a, a dedicated viewer
of Good Mythical Morning,

00:06:57.573 --> 00:07:00.020
if you're a fan of
Mythical Kitchen, you can,

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.779
you can get involved in those worlds

00:07:01.779 --> 00:07:04.867
and just kind of stay there.

00:07:04.867 --> 00:07:07.652
We're grappling with the
challenge of continuing

00:07:07.652 --> 00:07:11.300
to find ways to reach out
and introduce more people

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:14.722
to the world of mythical and
the things that we're doing.

00:07:14.722 --> 00:07:16.451
People have an idea of what,

00:07:16.451 --> 00:07:18.740
and an awareness of good mythical morning,

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:21.778
and they might, may dip in and out of it.

00:07:21.778 --> 00:07:23.988
But, we also want to
do things that continue

00:07:23.988 --> 00:07:25.544
to remind people.

00:07:25.544 --> 00:07:29.412
Hey, we're, we've still
got ideas and we want to,

00:07:29.412 --> 00:07:33.170
we want to make things
that express ourselves

00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:37.363
and also make us part of new conversations

00:07:37.363 --> 00:07:41.375
and introduce us to new mythical beasts.

00:07:41.375 --> 00:07:46.089
And I think above all it's
for, for both of us, it's,

00:07:46.089 --> 00:07:48.172
there's a creative passion,

00:07:48.172 --> 00:07:51.465
to that we don't want to, cause, again.

00:07:51.465 --> 00:07:53.043
You don't want to sit on your hands,

00:07:53.043 --> 00:07:54.230
You don't want to sit on your laurel.

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:55.541
Rest on your laurels.

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:56.558
Yes, we're the guys who eat weird things

00:07:56.558 --> 00:07:58.869
on the internet and do things.

00:07:58.869 --> 00:08:01.533
And you kind of see us in the
context of our friendship.

00:08:01.533 --> 00:08:05.137
Maybe that could be enough
for a lot of people, you know,

00:08:05.137 --> 00:08:06.903
for us, I don't think
it is because it's like,

00:08:06.903 --> 00:08:08.210
we got things that we want to create.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.625
We got worlds that we want to bring up.

00:08:09.625 --> 00:08:11.827
So, then the discussion started was like,

00:08:11.827 --> 00:08:13.024
what does that look
like? Because we've had,

00:08:13.024 --> 00:08:15.913
we've had a number of people,

00:08:15.913 --> 00:08:19.346
including like TV executives
who say things like, guys,

00:08:19.346 --> 00:08:21.009
if you have an idea for something,

00:08:21.009 --> 00:08:24.658
why don't you just make it
and put it on YouTube? Right.

00:08:24.658 --> 00:08:27.715
And I think there's a number of reasons

00:08:27.715 --> 00:08:29.565
why we've been hesitant to do that

00:08:29.565 --> 00:08:30.648
when it comes to narrative stuff,

00:08:30.648 --> 00:08:32.905
besides just like an
occasional sketch or whatever,

00:08:32.905 --> 00:08:36.529
which we're not really doing
that much on YouTube anymore.

00:08:36.529 --> 00:08:37.362
The reason being...

00:08:37.362 --> 00:08:38.195
But we are doing it on TikTok,

00:08:38.195 --> 00:08:39.273
and we'll talk about that later.

00:08:39.273 --> 00:08:43.105
Yeah. The reason being is
that with few exceptions,

00:08:43.105 --> 00:08:47.853
people are not really interacting
with narrative content on,

00:08:47.853 --> 00:08:50.853
on YouTube, in, in a meaningful way.

00:08:52.129 --> 00:08:53.350
Right? And you can be like, well,

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:55.065
you guys could change that,
but it's like, that's a,

00:08:55.065 --> 00:08:56.758
a tough hill to climb.

00:08:56.758 --> 00:09:00.080
What we were seeing is
that, you know what?

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:03.140
Kind of in an early sort
of YouTube way, the,

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:05.246
the, this early stage of TikTok,

00:09:05.246 --> 00:09:07.704
one of the things that's
happening is sketch comedy,

00:09:07.704 --> 00:09:09.521
just to use a broad term,

00:09:09.521 --> 00:09:12.488
has sort of found a
resurgence in this place.

00:09:12.488 --> 00:09:14.238
Like, scripted comedy

00:09:16.037 --> 00:09:18.597
has found a home on TikTok,

00:09:18.597 --> 00:09:21.243
and all of a sudden people are engaged.

00:09:21.243 --> 00:09:23.701
Our kids, are engaging with it in a way

00:09:23.701 --> 00:09:26.701
that they are not engaging with YouTube.

00:09:26.701 --> 00:09:30.368
In a way that's much more
broad than if you were to apply

00:09:30.368 --> 00:09:33.457
that same statement of
sketch comedy to Vine,

00:09:33.457 --> 00:09:34.290
back in the day.

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:35.123
Yeah.

00:09:35.123 --> 00:09:37.122
I never observed, maybe I missed it,

00:09:37.122 --> 00:09:40.338
because we never got
on the vine bandwagon.

00:09:40.338 --> 00:09:44.838
I never observed a type of
sketch that I wanted to do.

00:09:46.365 --> 00:09:51.365
It was, it was, it was very
short and very tonally specific.

00:09:51.711 --> 00:09:54.650
And there's a, there's a
broad range of content.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.467
I mean, there's, there's all,

00:09:56.467 --> 00:09:59.717
all niches now seem to exist on TikTok.

00:10:00.621 --> 00:10:04.490
I mean, spiritual deconstruction,
TikTok, as an example,

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:05.323
And Christian TikTok.

00:10:05.323 --> 00:10:06.156
Oh yeah.

00:10:06.156 --> 00:10:09.816
I mean, you name it, that
it, it's all happening there.

00:10:09.816 --> 00:10:11.694
And so there's like,

00:10:11.694 --> 00:10:13.652
it can melt into the world of podcasting

00:10:13.652 --> 00:10:15.841
and it can melt into the
world of sketch comedy.

00:10:15.841 --> 00:10:18.792
It can melt into the, of
course, the world of dance.

00:10:18.792 --> 00:10:20.902
Well, and, and, I, and I was doing some.

00:10:20.902 --> 00:10:22.166
And avant-guarde shit.

00:10:22.166 --> 00:10:23.395
So, all types of stuff.

00:10:23.395 --> 00:10:25.999
I don't remember... So, I
always kind of think, I was,

00:10:25.999 --> 00:10:29.641
I was sitting there trying
to figure out like, okay.

00:10:29.641 --> 00:10:32.755
Is there a way in for us that
kind of makes it, I mean,

00:10:32.755 --> 00:10:33.810
honestly it was kind of,

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:37.151
it was from a strategy
standpoint in terms of, yeah,

00:10:37.151 --> 00:10:38.352
we could do something that was,

00:10:38.352 --> 00:10:40.798
is just like just straight up comedy,

00:10:40.798 --> 00:10:43.663
like classic Rhett and Link
sketch in a narrative fashion,

00:10:43.663 --> 00:10:45.212
as you see. And we'll talk about later,

00:10:45.212 --> 00:10:46.682
we are doing classic Rhett and Link sketch

00:10:46.682 --> 00:10:48.620
sort of individually on TikTok

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:52.070
and learning a lot over
there, but like, how do you,

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:53.903
we want to do something
that's more eventized

